  "goodToKnow": "Der Torwart is a goalkeeper: synonyms are der Torhüter and der Keeper, and in Austria der Tormann. Germany has a strong goalkeeping tradition, from Sepp Maier and Oliver Kahn to Manuel Neuer, who reshaped the role as a sweeper-keeper. Den Ball halten means to save it; ein Eigentor is an own goal. The old word Wart means guard or keeper, as in der Hauswart (caretaker). Plural: die Torwarte or die Torwärter."
